On 19.08.2019 04:10, Xiaofeng Ren wrote:
> Anyone can help to provide some suggestion about following kernelci=20
> integration problem:
> We setup one kernelci in our infrastructure and deploy LAVA master and=
=20
> slave as well. kernelci can support build, LAVA can also work to run=20
> automation test. We use the lava-boot-v2.sh (jenkins job in=20
> kernelci-core project ) to trigger lava test, but we found that both=20
> boot report or test report can't be synchronized to kernelci=20
> dashboard. It will report json format error, may I know whether we=20
> need follow boot schema or test schema defined in kernelci=20
> (https://api.kernelci.org/schema-boot.html=C2=A0and=20
> https://api.kernelci.org/schema-test.html) to create one report, then=20
> trigger LAVA callback function to post one request?
>
In general /callback endpoint is meant to be used to upload LAVA test=20
results to KernelCI. It should be called by LAVA after the test job is=20
completed.

Can you see if /callback URL is being called by LAVA after the test job=20
is done?

> Following is callback definition in=20
> https://github.com/kernelci/kernelci-core/blob/master/templates/base/ker=
nel-ci-base.jinja2.=20
> Do we need customize this callback if we want to post request for boot=
=20
> and test result?=C2=A0 Any suggestion will be appreciated.
> {%- if callback %}
>
> =09notify:
>
> =09criteria:
>
> =09status: finished
>
> =09callback:
>
> =09{%- if callback_type =3D=3D 'custom' %}
>
> =09url: {{ callback_url }}
>
> =09{%- else %}
>
> =09url: {{ callback_url }}/callback/{{ callback_name }}?lab_name=3D{{=20
> lab_name }}&status=3D{STATUS}&status_string=3D{STATUS_STRING}
>
> =09{%- endif %}
>
> =09method: POST
>
> =09dataset: {{ callback_dataset }}
>
> =09token: {{ callback }}
>
> =09content-type: json
>
> =09{% endif %}
>
>=20

